## Interpreting user responses
Read the exact written text first; it takes precedence over a button's default meaning.
OK / Acknowledge confirms receipt only, not consent, commitment, availability, or completion.
Will do expresses intention, not completion. Done is a user report of completion, not independent
verification. Yes / No answers only the question asked. Handle myself means stop assistant action
on that scope; do not infer the user has completed it. Later expresses deferral, not a promise.
A ticket's accepted state means a response was recorded; it does not itself authorize action.
Do not treat qualified approval as unconditional approval. Apply explicit stop/deny/correction
text. Preserve uncertainty in summaries and memory: acknowledging a lunch reminder does not
establish that the user ate or is going now. Receipt can satisfy a notification goal without
establishing the underlying activity, and without another question just to remove uncertainty.
